---
description: >-
  label-syntax.mmd with markdownAlwaysOn: every label is markdown, so the
  plain **bold** _ital_ rows of every kind (namespace title, class label,
  member, method, relation label and note) draw bold and italic, the
  code-span and bare-backtick rows draw inline code, and the method written
  with a markdown string draws its backticks as a code span. Tags, \n and
  the markdown strings draw as in label-syntax.mmd, so the picture differs
  from it (#1368, #1389).
config:
  markdownAlwaysOn: true
---
classDiagram
  direction LR
  namespace N1["namespace **bold** _ital_"] {
    class A1["class **bold** _ital_"] {
      +member **bold** _ital_
      +method **bold** _ital_()
    }
  }
  A1 --> B1 : relation **bold** _ital_
  note for A1 "note **bold** _ital_"
  namespace N2["`namespace **bold** _ital_`"] {
    class A2["`class **bold** _ital_`"] {
      +"`member **bold** _ital_`"
      +"`method **bold** _ital_`"()
    }
  }
  A2 --> B2 : "`relation **bold** _ital_`"
  note for A2 "`note **bold** _ital_`"
  namespace N3 {
    class A3 {
      +`member **bold** _ital_`
      +`method **bold** _ital_`()
    }
  }
  A3 --> B3 : `relation **bold** _ital_`
  namespace N4["namespace a `code` b"] {
    class A4["class a `code` b"] {
      +member a `code` b
      +method a `code` b()
    }
  }
  A4 --> B4 : relation a `code` b
  note for A4 "note a `code` b"
  namespace N5["namespace <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"] {
    class A5["class <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"] {
      +member <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
      +method <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O()
    }
  }
  A5 --> B5 : relation <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O
  note for A5 "note <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O"
  namespace N6["namespace one\ntwo"] {
    class A6["class one\ntwo"] {
      +member one\ntwo
      +method one\ntwo()
    }
  }
  A6 --> B6 : relation one\ntwo
  note for A6 "note one\ntwo"
